DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uussbbhhiidd library provides routines to extract data from USB Human In‐
     terface Devices.

   IInnttrroodduuccttiioonn
     USB HID devices send and receive data laid out in a device dependent way.
     The uussbbhhiidd library contains routines to extract the _r_e_p_o_r_t _d_e_s_c_r_i_p_t_o_r
     which contains the data layout information and then use this information.

     The routines can be divided into four parts: extraction of the descrip‐
     tor, parsing of the descriptor, translating to/from symbolic names, and
     data manipulation.

   SSyynncchhrroonnoouuss HHIIDD ooppeerraattiioonn
     Synchronous HID operation can be enabled or disabled by a call to
     hhiidd__sseett__iimmmmeedd().  If the second argument is zero synchronous HID opera‐
     tion is disabled.  Else synchronous HID operation is enabled.  The func‐
     tion returns a negative value on failure.

     hhiidd__ggeett__rreeppoorrtt() and hhiidd__sseett__rreeppoorrtt() functions allow to synchronously
     get and set specific report if device supports it.  For devices with mul‐
     tiple report IDs, wanted ID should be provided in the first byte of the
     buffer for both get and set.

   DDeessccrriippttoorr FFuunnccttiioonnss
     The report descriptor ID can be obtained by calling hhiidd__ggeett__rreeppoorrtt__iidd().
     A report descriptor can be obtained by calling hhiidd__ggeett__rreeppoorrtt__ddeesscc() with
     a file descriptor obtained by opening a uhid(4) device.  Alternatively a
     data buffer containing the report descriptor can be passed into
     hhiidd__uussee__rreeppoorrtt__ddeesscc().  The data is copied into an internal structure.
     When the report descriptor is no longer needed it should be freed by
     calling hhiidd__ddiissppoossee__rreeppoorrtt__ddeesscc().  The type _r_e_p_o_r_t___d_e_s_c___t is opaque and
     should be used when calling the parsing functions.  If
     hhiidd__ddiissppoossee__rreeppoorrtt__ddeesscc() fails it will return NULL.

   DDeessccrriippttoorr PPaarrssiinngg FFuunnccttiioonnss
     To parse the report descriptor the hhiidd__ssttaarrtt__ppaarrssee() function should be
     called with a report descriptor, a set that describes which items that
     are interesting, and the desired report ID (or -1 to obtain items of all
     report IDs).  The set is obtained by OR-ing together values _(_1 _<_< _k_)
     where _k is an item of type _h_i_d___k_i_n_d___t.  The function returns NULL if the
     initialization fails, otherwise an opaque value to be used in subsequent
     calls.  After parsing the hhiidd__eenndd__ppaarrssee() function should be called to
     free internal data structures.

     To iterate through all the items in the report descriptor hhiidd__ggeett__iitteemm()
     should be called while it returns a value greater than 0.  When the re‐
     port descriptor ends it will returns 0; a syntax error within the report
     descriptor will cause a return value less than 0.  The struct pointed to
     by _h will be filled with the relevant data for the item.  The definition
     of _h_i_d___i_t_e_m___t can be found in <_u_s_b_h_i_d_._h> and the meaning of the compo‐
     nents in the USB HID documentation.

     Data should be read/written to the device in the size of the report.  The
     size of a report (of a certain kind) can be computed by the
     hhiidd__rreeppoorrtt__ssiizzee() function.  If the report is prefixed by an ID byte it
     is given by _i_d.

     To locate a single item the hhiidd__llooccaattee() function can be used.  It should
     be given the usage code of the item and its kind and it will fill the
     item and return non-zero if the item was found.

   NNaammee TTrraannssllaattiioonn FFuunnccttiioonnss
     The function hhiidd__uussaaggee__ppaaggee() will return the symbolic name of a usage
     page, and the function hhiidd__uussaaggee__iinn__ppaaggee() will return the symbolic name
     of the usage within the page.  Both these functions may return a pointer
     to static data.

     The functions hhiidd__ppaarrssee__uussaaggee__ppaaggee() and hhiidd__ppaarrssee__uussaaggee__iinn__ppaaggee() are
     the inverses of hhiidd__uussaaggee__ppaaggee() and hhiidd__uussaaggee__iinn__ppaaggee().  They take a
     usage string and return the number of the usage, or -1 if it cannot be
     found.

     Before any of these functions can be called the usage table must be
     parsed, this is done by calling hhiidd__iinniitt() with the name of the table.
     Passing NULL to this function will cause it to use the default table.

   DDaattaa EExxttrraaccttiioonn FFuunnccttiioonnss
     Given the data obtained from a HID device and an item in the report de‐
     scriptor the hhiidd__ggeett__ddaattaa() function extracts the value of the item.
     Conversely hhiidd__sseett__ddaattaa() can be used to put data into a report (which
     must be zeroed first).

